  "1e_summary": {
    "finding": "the two valid measures agree PERFECTLY along any single dephasing trajectory in every dimension -- that is the ordering the front actually needs, since resolution moves a state along one such path. They disagree on a growing fraction of pairs when comparing UNRELATED states, and the disagreement grows with d. So thickness is well defined as a monotone along a resolution history, and NOT well defined as an absolute cross-system quantity above d = 2.",
    "consequence": "the framework may say \"this cell thinned\" without choosing a measure, but may not say \"cell A is thicker than cell B\" for unrelated A and B without choosing one"
  }
